{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall serve YHWH your Elohim.</b> Corresponding to what the worshippers of idolatry, whom he mentioned above, think — that through that worship they will attain all their desire and their constellation will prevail and success and blessing in the work of their hands will come to them — he now mentions ועבדתם את ה״ אלהיכם, that it is not fitting for you to serve any but the Name designated uniquely, from whom blessing and all benefit come to you. That is what he says: וברך את לחמך ואת מימיך. <br><b>And I will remove illness from your midst.</b> There are illnesses within the body caused by foods and drink that enter the body, and there are illnesses outside the body caused by change of the air in accordance with the variation of the alignment of the stars. Therefore Scripture promises that with Torah and worship the Blessed One will bless a person's sustenance so that it will have the power of its nature to remove illnesses from him; and with this promise, one who fulfills the Torah will not need a physician. And this is what is written (II Chronicles 16:12): ״וגם בחליו לא דרש את ה׳ כי ברופאים״. Also included in 'illness' is that there be in them no intellect or principle — which is illness in man. And know that Scripture should properly say והסיר (as it says וברך), but the verse illuminates that Elohim will remove illness from our midst when we serve the designated Name and direct all forms of worship to the designated Name. And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:25.500731301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}